WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.040
Okay, so error handling in AI agents breaks when a tool fails,

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.267
because the agent gets a raw error string and improvises.

3
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.607
It might retry a charge that already went through,

4
00:00:11.607 --> 00:00:13.733
so the customer pays twice.

5
00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:18.513
So I'd classify each error first and let my code pick the recovery,

6
00:00:18.513 --> 00:00:19.567
not the model.

7
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:23.027
A transient error like a rate limit gets retried,

8
00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:28.133
and a permanent one like an invalid API key fails fast.

9
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.753
A timeout is ambiguous,

10
00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:31.953
since the server may have processed it,

11
00:00:31.953 --> 00:00:34.553
so I'd attach an idempotency key,

12
00:00:34.553 --> 00:00:37.313
which makes the tool safe to call twice.
